# Eutopia PG vs PePG — sharded by (seed, combo) (HTCondor array)
#
# One (seed, reward, constraint) triple per job -- no internal multiprocessing
# pool, so no intra-shard worker contention. Use this instead of
# eutopia_array.sub when you want the cleanest possible per-episode timing to
# study training curves: the seed-sharded array packs 8 combos onto one host
# at once and they visibly slow each other down as they all become CPU-active
# (measured drift: a fixed combo went 46.6s -> 57.5s/ep purely from sibling
# load; combos starting later in the same shard ran ~1.8x slower than the
# first ones). Splitting one combo per job removes that: every job gets its
# own host.
#
# jobs = 2 agents x N_SEEDS x 13 combos. Export N_SEEDS, N_JOBS (= 2*N_SEEDS*13),
# CAMPAIGN, and (if not using the 500/1000 defaults) TRAIN_EPISODES/
# DEPLOY_EPISODES before submitting -- e.g. for 10 seeds, 1000 train +
# 3000 deploy episodes:
#   export N_SEEDS=10 N_JOBS=260 CAMPAIGN=run10 TRAIN_EPISODES=1000 DEPLOY_EPISODES=3000
#   condor_submit_bid 25 eutopia_combo_array.sub
#
#   $(Process)  0 .. N_SEEDS*13-1        -> pepg
#   $(Process)  N_SEEDS*13 .. 2*N_SEEDS*13-1 -> pg
#
# The index -> (agent, seed, reward, constraint) arithmetic is done in
# run_job.sh's `combo` branch, NOT here -- same $CHOICE/$INT nesting limit as
# eutopia_array.sub. `queue` below reads N_JOBS from the environment, so
# there's nothing in this file to hand-edit per run.
#
# THEN, once all jobs have finished (condor_q shows none left), aggregate
# (must export the SAME N_SEEDS/CAMPAIGN/TRAIN_EPISODES/DEPLOY_EPISODES used
# above):
#   export N_SEEDS=10 CAMPAIGN=run10 TRAIN_EPISODES=1000 DEPLOY_EPISODES=3000
#   ~/LoanSimulator/cluster/run_job.sh pepg aggregate
#   ~/LoanSimulator/cluster/run_job.sh pg   aggregate
#
# No editing needed: $ENV(HOME) is expanded by HTCondor at submit time.

executable = $ENV(HOME)/LoanSimulator/cluster/run_job.sh
arguments  = combo $(Process)

output = $ENV(HOME)/eutopia_logs/combo_$(ClusterId).$(Process).out
error  = $ENV(HOME)/eutopia_logs/combo_$(ClusterId).$(Process).err
log    = $ENV(HOME)/eutopia_logs/combo_$(ClusterId).log

initialdir = $ENV(HOME)/LoanSimulator

# One (seed, combo) job = one Python process, no internal pool. A single
# population (12000+12000) + policy net + the 100k-row data load is far
# lighter than the 8-worker shard's 32GB ask. Memory footprint doesn't grow
# with episode count -- per-episode history is plain scalars appended to a
# list, and the replay buffer is capped -- so this is unchanged regardless of
# TRAIN_EPISODES/DEPLOY_EPISODES.
request_cpus   = 2
request_memory = 8192
request_disk   = 5242880
request_gpus   = 0

getenv = True

# Jobs are idempotent -- a retry re-reads its own existing checkpoint (if any)
# and skips recomputing it.
max_retries = 3

queue $ENV(N_JOBS)
